       <p>Death caps and destroying angels are among the amatoxin-producing <em>Amanita</em> groups. An important warning combination is pale or white free gills and usually white spores, a fragile stem ring that may be absent with age, a cap that may be white, green, yellow, or brown, and a bulb or saclike volva at the base that may be hidden underground. Any feature may be damaged, lost, or obscured.<sup class="citation-marker">[S05][S07][S08]</sup></p>
