       <p>Michigan guidance treats false morels such as <em>Gyromitra</em> as poisonous and not edible. True morels have definite pits and are hollow; false morels may be wrinkled, lobed, waved, brainlike, or chambered. This structural comparison helps flag risk but does not certify a collection as edible.<sup class="citation-marker">[S09]</sup></p>
